  <data name="Tutorial_Connection_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Type the phone's IP, or press Scan to auto-discover devices. Pick one from the list, then Connect to start streaming its live data.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Connection_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Connect a watch</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_DoneButton" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Done ✓</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Export_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Export any session to CSV for analysis. The trivia question bank is managed from the Trivia button right next to it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Export_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Export your data</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Finish_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You're ready to run a session. Press this Tutorial button whenever you'd like to see these tips again. Good luck!</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Finish_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>That's the tour! 🚀</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Intervention_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Manually fire a notification or mini-game (trivia, Simon Says, …) to the watch every intervention you trigger is logged as research data.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Intervention_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Send an intervention</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Motion_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A live 3D model of the wrist plus the reconstructed motion trail. The little heart up here beats in time with the participant's current BPM, so you can read heart rate at a glance while watching their movement.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Motion_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Motion &amp; rotation tracker</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Runner_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Drive the experiment on the watch: start, pause, step between events and follow the live countdown for the active task.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Runner_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Experiment runner</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Scan_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scan now finds both Wi-Fi devices broadcasting on the network and any phone attached over USB debugging a USB connection is folded in, not overwritten.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Scan_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scan for devices</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Sensors_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The raw real-time read-outs heart rate and per-axis accelerometer deltas straight off the watch.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_Sensors_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Live sensors</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_SessionName_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Give each recording session a clear name (e.g. the participant code). It's stored alongside every data row you later export.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_SessionName_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Name your session</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_SkipButton" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Skip tour</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_StartStop_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When you're set up, Start Session begins recording and Stop Session ends it. Notes you type during a run are saved against the session.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tutorial_StartStop_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Start &amp; stop recording</value>
  </data>
